# Cursor AI Agent Rules

## Auto-approval Rules with 5-second delay
- Wait 5 seconds before auto-approving file operations (create, edit, delete, move)
- Wait 5 seconds before auto-approving terminal commands unless they involve:
  - System-level changes (sudo, rm -rf /, etc.)
  - Network operations that could be dangerous
  - Database operations that could cause data loss
- Auto-approve code formatting and linting fixes after 5 seconds
- Auto-approve dependency installations after 5 seconds
- Show countdown timer for user awareness

## File Operations
- You can create, edit, delete files without asking for permission
- You can modify existing files to improve code quality
- You can reorganize project structure if it improves maintainability
- Always backup important files before major changes

## Terminal Commands
- Run build commands automatically (npm run build, etc.)
- Run test commands automatically
- Run linting and formatting commands
- Install dependencies when needed
- Ask for confirmation only for potentially dangerous operations

## Code Quality
- Always format code on save
- Fix linting errors automatically
- Organize imports automatically
- Add proper error handling
- Follow best practices for the language/framework

## Safety Guidelines
- Never run commands that could damage the system
- Always test changes in a safe environment
- Create backups before major refactoring
- Ask for confirmation for operations involving:
  - Database schema changes
  - API key or credential modifications
  - Production deployments
  - Large-scale file deletions

## Communication
- Be proactive in suggesting improvements
- Explain what you're doing and why
- Provide clear feedback on changes made
- Ask questions when requirements are unclear